\HarfBuzz\ (\url{https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz}) is a text \emph{shaping}
engine: it takes Unicode characters and a font and outputs positioned glyphs.
It is the industry-standard open-source solution for text shaping, relied upon
by billions of users in browsers, operating systems, and word processors\Dash and
essential for complex scripts such as Arabic and Indic that require reordering,
ligatures, and other transformations.

This article traces the evolution of digital text shaping and the formation of
\HarfBuzz, the parallel evolution of \TeX\ engines toward Unicode and complex
scripts, their integration with \HarfBuzz, and a vision for the future of fonts
and shaping.
